{
 "id": "passive",
 "title": "La voix passive",
 "level": "B1",
 "topic": "Grammaire",
 "summary": "be + participe passé : quand l'utiliser, comment la former à tous les temps, et le complément d'agent « by ».",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Quand l'employer ?"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "Quand l'**agent est inconnu** ou sans importance : *My laptop was stolen.*",
    "Quand l'**action** est plus importante que celui qui la fait : *The database is backed up every night.*",
    "Dans les textes **formels** et **techniques** : *The server was restarted.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Formation"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "**sujet + be (au temps voulu) + participe passé** (+ by + agent)."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "head": [
    "Temps",
    "Actif",
    "Passif"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "présent simple",
     "They fix bugs.",
     "Bugs are fixed."
    ],
    [
     "prétérit",
     "They fixed the bug.",
     "The bug was fixed."
    ],
    [
     "present perfect",
     "They have fixed it.",
     "It has been fixed."
    ],
    [
     "futur",
     "They will fix it.",
     "It will be fixed."
    ],
    [
     "modal",
     "You must fix it.",
     "It must be fixed."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Le complément d'agent"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "On ajoute **by** seulement si l'agent est important : *The vulnerability was discovered **by a researcher**.*"
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Verbes à deux compléments"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "*They gave me a badge.* → *I was given a badge.* (plus naturel que *A badge was given to me.*)"
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "The files are stored in the cloud.",
   "fr": "Les fichiers sont stockés dans le cloud."
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "The email was sent yesterday.",
   "fr": "Le mail a été envoyé hier."
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "The system has been updated.",
   "fr": "Le système a été mis à jour."
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "The meeting will be held on Friday.",
   "fr": "La réunion aura lieu vendredi."
  },
  {
   "type": "tip",
   "text": "**Piège** : le français utilise « on » (*on a volé mon portable*). L'anglais préfère le passif : *My phone was stolen.*"
  }
 ],
